{{Quote|We are Alderaan. We answer rage with wisdom. We answer fear with imagination. We answer war with hope. If one life with a single drop of Alderaanian blood survives, Alderaan survives. If one life with a passion for Alderaanian creativity survives, Alderaan survives. And we are, each of us, important. And whatever happens, I bow to all of you&mdash;and to our future.|Princess Leia Organa, after the destruction of Alderaan|<ref name="Princess Leia 5">[[Princess Leia 5|''Princess Leia'' 5]]</ref>}}
'''Alderaanians''' were a cultural group of [[human]]s [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Alderaan]].<ref name="Leia 4" /> Known for their pacifistic values and devotion to the arts, prominent individuals included [[Viceroy]] [[Bail Prestor Organa]] and his [[Marriage|wife]], [[Alderaanian monarchy|Queen]] [[Breha Organa]], who were the adoptive [[parent]]s of [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]].<ref name="Revenge of the Sith">{{Film|III}}</ref> They were driven to the brink of extinction by the destruction of their homeworld by the [[Galactic Empire]] via the original [[Death Star]]<ref name="Leia 1" /> in [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]''</ref> with only a few scattered remnants across the galaxy being all that remained of the pacifistic people.<ref name="Leia 1" />

==Biology and appearance==
The Alderaanians were a [[Subspecies|race]] of [[human]]s native to the [[planet]] [[Alderaan]]. While majority of individuals had skin [[Color|tones]] like reddish tan, golden tan and dark brown,<ref name="Leia 1" /><ref name="Sanctuary">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 4: Sanctuary}}</ref> some like the adopted [[Princess]]<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /> [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] had more pale skin.<ref name="Leia 1" />

==Society and culture==
The Alderaanians were a pacifist society, one devoted to the fine arts and to philosophy, and freely shared their knowledge with others. They were also careful to live in harmony with their [[planet]], which was renowned for its untarnished beauty.<ref name="Leia 2">[[Princess Leia 2|''Princess Leia'' 2]]</ref>

Alderaan also had a [[Alderaanian monarchy|monarchy]]<ref name="A New Hope">{{Film|IV}}</ref> that was dedicated to the welfare of its people and had existed for thousands of years.<ref name="Leia Princess of Alderaan">''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]''</ref>

Alderaan had a number of traditions about [[braid]]s such as who wore them, when, and why that vaired from continent to continent and age to age. The [[monarch of Alderaan]] was expected to wear braids.<ref name="Leia Princess of Alderaan" /> Some Alderaanian [[Gender|males]], like [[Nash Windrider]] wore their [[hair]] long by tradition.<ref name="Lost Stars">''[[Lost Stars]]''</ref>

==History==
===Natives of Alderaan===
[[File:BailBrehaOrgana-TSWB.png|thumb|250px|Alderaanian monarchs Queen Breha Organa and Viceroy Bail Organa.]]
Early in their history, the Alderaanians employed [[soldier]]s like most other cultures, before gradually developing into a pacifist society. Over [[time]], Alderaanians became noted for sharing their knowledge with the rest of the [[Galactic community]].<ref name="Leia 2" />

Throughout history, a number of Alderaanians emigrated to other planets, founding communities and exporting their unique culture far from their [[homeworld]]. Such offworld communities notably existed on [[Naboo]]<ref name="Leia 2" /> and [[Sullust]].<ref name="Leia 3">[[Princess Leia 3|''Princess Leia'' 3]]</ref> Generations before the [[Galactic Civil War]], a number of Alderaanians also established their presence on the planet of [[Espirion]], which was known for being open to [[refugee]]s and wanderers. There, they intermarried with the [[Espirion (species)|natives]], a [[species]] of [[Color|red]]-skinned [[humanoid]]s with tapered [[ear]]s. As a result, a population of [[Alder-Espirion|half-Alderaanians]], exhibiting non-human characteristics, arose on Espirion. In the immediate aftermath of the [[Battle of Yavin]], their community was led by [[Chief]] [[Beon Beonel]].<ref name="Leia 4" />

===People without a planet===
{{Quote|As we ''speak'', the Imperials are hunting down all surviving Alderaanians.''"<br />"''All? How do you know?''"<br />"''Word travels through the Rebel forces. Too much so to simply be rumor.|Evaan Verlaine and Leia Organa|<ref name="Leia 1" />}}
When Alderaan was [[Destruction of Alderaan|destroyed]] by the [[Galactic Empire]] to test the capabilities of their new [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[battle station]], most Alderaanians perished along with their home planet. Those who survived by being offworld were targeted<ref name="SWSquadrons">''[[Star Wars: Squadrons]]''</ref> for extermination by the Empire in a [[Purge of Alderaanians|purge]],<ref name="Outlaws">''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]''</ref> albeit with some exceptions such as the Imperial loyalist [[Nash Windrider]]<ref name="Lost Stars">''[[Lost Stars]]''</ref> and the Imperial [[Admiral]] [[Gallia Kryder]], who survived the purge by moving her [[Gallia Kryder's fleet|fleet]] to the edge of [[Wild Space]].<ref name="Outlaws" /> Shortly after the Battle of [[Yavin Prime|Yavin]], during which the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] retaliated against the Empire and destroyed the Death Star, a [[Alderaanian refugee convoy|convoy]] of refugees was [[Battle at Fostar Haven|rescued]] by [[Echo Squadron]].<ref name="SWSquadrons" /> [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] set off on a [[Mission to rescue the survivors of Alderaan|mission]] to rescue the surviving sons and daughters of Alderaan.<ref name="Leia 1" />

Some Alderaanians who served in the Alliance to Restore the Republic wore a [[Tear|tattoo]] of the [[Rebel Alliance starbird]] beneath their left eye to symbolise the planet they came from and the people they lost.<ref name="Chapter 12: The Siege">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 12: The Siege}}</ref> This became widespread enough that Imperial veterans were able to recognize the tattoo on sight and know that the wearer came from Alderaan, as was the case with an Imperial shuttle [[Unidentified Imperial shuttle co-pilot|pilot]] confronted by [[Carasynthia Dune]].<ref name="Chapter 16: The Rescue">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 16: The Rescue}}</ref>

